Dear list,

While working on barebox recently, I decided to port a couple of patches =
=A0I made to an old barebox tree a few years ago, to fix the IDE ports =
on the x86 platform.

I had to work on the resource allocation a bit, as the current GIT =
repository does not allow IORESOURCE_IO type to be passed to =
dev_request_region( ) and friends. I tried to keep the interface the =
same as much as possible by using macros etc.
Please find that attached in =
0001-common-driver-Allow-for-I-O-mapped-I-O-in-resource-r.patch.=20

Next, I added support to the platform IDE interface to use I/O-mapped =
I/O, and added the necessary allocation to the generic_pc board.

I did have to add a call to ata_port_detect( ) to ide_port_register to =
actually get the drives to be probed. Without it the interface seems to =
be stuck in some sort of limbo. This patch is in =
0002-x86-Add-support-for-IDE-on-the-legacy-I-O-ports.patch.

Lastly, I added an extra serial port to the generic_pc board. Most =
(legacy) PCs have support for 2 serial ports, it seemed useful to me.

What does puzzle me is that the arch/x86/boot/Kconfig mentions X86_VESA =
and X86_VGA support, but the files (console_vga.c and console_vesa.c) do =
not nor have ever existed. Is this a remnant from U-boot v1?

Best regards,

Michel Stam

